  "findings": [
    "Substituting r=k+11 into the fixed-gap bound yields 2*B*S*[D*(k+12)]^(k+11), where B=2*C*A, S=F+H0 and D=2*B/rho. Positive rho and nonnegative coefficients justify multiplication by the numeric bound.",
    "Power splitting yields exactly Cstar=2*B*Ebox*D^11*3^12*12^11 and Astar=D*6144. These depend only on supplied rho,C,A,Ebox; neither depends on k, x or the chosen set point. S=F+H0 remains a multiplicative amplitude.",
    "No division by S or Ebox occurs. Zero amplitude and zero embedding coefficient cause no algebraic exception. The all-order arithmetic includes k=0.",
    "The final norm family theorem retains hshift: for every k and x in K, norm(J k x)<=Ebox*N(k+11,rho), with a single common Ebox. Bare Norm suffices because only that real comparison is used; no unproved norm positivity or Sobolev properties are inferred.",
    "The explicit fixed-gap recurrence hrec, nonnegative shrinking-region family, monotonicity, base bound through order eight and actual R24 comparison remain premises. This is a conditional formal implication and does not prove weighted PDE recurrence, Sobolev embedding or physical analyticity."
  ],
